---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Start Here | Aging at Home Lab" description="Start with the Aging at Home Lab master checklist for making an older adult's home safer and easier to care for.">
  <article class="prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">Start Here</p>
    <h1>Start with the home safety and caregiver organization basics.</h1>
    <p>If you are helping an older adult stay at home, the first step is not buying products. The first step is understanding what needs attention: walking paths, bathroom safety, lighting, medication information, emergency contacts, and family responsibilities.</p>

    <div class="callout warning">
      <h2>Draft resource notice</h2>
      <p>The flagship checklist is currently being source-verified and prepared for publication. It should be treated as a draft planning resource until final citations and review are complete.</p>
    </div>

    <h2>The first three questions</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Can the person move through the home safely during normal daily routines?</li>
      <li>Can they call for help from the places where problems are most likely to happen?</li>
      <li>Does the family have the information needed to act quickly in an emergency?</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>Recommended first resources</h2>
    <div class="grid">
      <section class="card">
        <h3>Complete Aging-in-Place Checklist</h3>
        <p>The cornerstone guide for identifying what to fix first and what may need professional review.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="card">
        <h3>Family Caregiver Binder</h3>
        <p>A practical system for keeping emergency contacts, medications, doctors, appointments, and care notes in one place.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="card">
        <h3>Room-by-Room Safety Audit</h3>
        <p>A structured way to walk through the home without missing bathrooms, bedrooms, stairs, lighting, and entryways.</p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
